Checking StyleBro's rules, xunit.analyzers' assertion rules where they are warnings or errors and the built-in rules init and migrate turn on (162 ids), changing nothing; --all checks every analyzer's and compiler fix too.
Held back: IDE0049: this .NET SDK's 'dotnet format' ignores the suppressor StyleBro's multi-target guard uses for IDE rules, so their fixes could write C# or APIs that another target framework or project compiling the same file doesn't have. They aren't applied here; a newer .NET SDK's 'dotnet format' applies them where the guard allows.
Multi-targeted: one 'dotnet format' run per target framework (net472, net8.0, netstandard2.0). net10.0: no run of its own, the code compiles the same as for another framework of the same kind (the same '#if' symbols tested, files and settings).
Checked netstandard2.0 (run 1 of 3)
